---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="OpenIT · Privacy">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Last updated May 2026.</p>

  <h2>What stays on your machine</h2>
  <p>
    Everything in your OpenIT vault lives in files you own: tasks, knowledge
    articles, reports, commands, files, people, agents, scripts, and
    conversation history. Nothing leaves your Mac unless you explicitly share
    it, put the vault in a synced folder, or connect a third-party integration.
  </p>

  <h2>What goes to Anthropic</h2>
  <p>
    OpenIT uses Claude Code as its substrate. Prompts and the surrounding
    context that Claude Code chooses to include are sent to Anthropic per
    Anthropic's <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/policies/terms-of-service">terms of service</a>.
    OpenIT does not add additional telemetry on top of Claude's.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing a vault with your team</h2>
  <p>
    OpenIT is built for small teams to share one vault. If you put the vault
    in a synced folder like Google Drive, Dropbox, or git, its contents
    sync through that service per its terms, and everyone you share the folder
    with can read and edit those files. OpenIT itself adds no server in
    between; the sync is whatever tool you already use.
  </p>

  <h2>CLI tools and MCP servers</h2>
  <p>
    When Claude runs CLI tools (<code>gh</code>, <code>aws</code>, etc.) or
    MCP servers you've installed, those tools communicate with their
    respective services using your existing credentials. OpenIT doesn't
    intercept or log this traffic.
  </p>

  <h2>Crash + error telemetry</h2>
  <p>None. If we add it, we'll update this page first.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions: open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/openit-app/openit-app/issues">GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
